<article class="env-lemma" id="094H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/094H">Lemma <span data-tag="094H">21.53.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring. Let $K, L \in D^-(\mathcal{C}, \Lambda )$. If the cohomology sheaves of $K$ and $L$ are locally constant sheaves of $\Lambda $-modules of finite type, then the cohomology sheaves of $K \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} L$ are locally constant sheaves of $\Lambda $-modules of finite type. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We'll prove this as an application of Lemma <a href="/tag/094G" data-tag="094G">21.53.1</a>. Note that $H^ i(K \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} L)$ is the same as $H^ i(\tau _{\geq i - 1}K \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} \tau _{\geq i - 1}L)$. Thus we may assume $K$ and $L$ are bounded. By Lemma <a href="/tag/094G" data-tag="094G">21.53.1</a> we may assume that $K$ and $L$ are represented by complexes of locally constant sheaves of $\Lambda $-modules of finite type. Then we can replace these complexes by bounded above complexes of finite free $\Lambda $-modules. In this case the result is clear. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>